            "ImageDescription": {
              "value": "Thomas Baines. Climbing the Heights of the Drakensberg, 31 May 1871. Watercolour and pencil on paper. According to the artist\u2019s inscription, the work was \u201cpainted by candlelight\u201d and intended to be viewed under similar lighting conditions. The scene relates to Baines\u2019s travel notes during his journey near the Bushman\u2019s River.\n<p>Quote from the diary:\n</p>\n\u201cSaturday, 27th. Crossed Bushman's River Bridge and Little Bushman's River. Found Mr. Zeller, the Portuguese consul-general, who is going to the Transvaal to annul all the boundary treaties Senhor Barrahona de Costa has made.\u201d",
              "source": "commons-desc-page"
            },
            "DateTimeOriginal": {
              "value": "31 May 1871",
              "source": "commons-desc-page"
            },
            "Credit": {
